      "standard_id": "MI2CAST",
      "name": "MI2CAST (Minimum Information about a Molecular Interaction Causal Statement)",
      "description": "A rule-based reporting guideline for annotating directed causal interactions between biological entities (source → effect → target). Defines four mandatory/optional rules covering (1) source/target identifiers, (2) causal relationship, (3) provenance/evidence, and (4) contextual details (biological activity/mechanism, taxon, compartment, cell/tissue, modifications, experimental setup). Recommends specific identifier systems and ontologies (e.g., UniProt/Ensembl/RNAcentral/CHEBI, PSI‑MI/RO for relation types, ECO for evidence, GO, NCBI taxonomy, CL, BRENDA, Sequence Ontology) and provides example encodings and formats (causalJSON, PSI‑MITAB examples, BEL examples). Intended as minimum metadata standard for curators, experimentalists and data users of molecular causal interaction data."
    }
  ],
